{"total":139,"totalPage":3,"page":3,"pageSize":50,"items":[{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd41","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2824,"bookHadithIndex":98,"text":"Narrated Salim and Hamzah, the sons of 'Abdullah bin 'Umar:from their father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"An omen is in three: A woman, a dwelling, and a (riding) beast","grades":[]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd42","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2824,"bookHadithIndex":98,"text":"Narrated Salim and Hamzah, the sons of 'Abdullah bin 'Umar:from their father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"An omen is in three: A woman, a dwelling, and a (riding) beast","grades":[]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd43","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2825,"bookHadithIndex":99,"text":"Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whenever there are three of you, then let two not converse in exclusion of their companion","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2825-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2825-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2825-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2825-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd44","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2826,"bookHadithIndex":100,"text":"Narrated Isma'il bin Abi Khalid:that Abu Juhaifah said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (he was) white and turning grey. Al-Hasan bin 'Ali resembles him most. He had promised thirteen young she-camels for us, so we went to get them. When we arrived he had died without giving us anything. So when Abu Bakr (became the Khalifah) he said: 'If there is anyone to whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made a promise, then let him come forth.' I stood to inform him about it, and he ordered that they be given to us","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2826-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2826-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2826-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd45","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2827,"bookHadithIndex":101,"text":"Narrated Isma'il bin Abi Khalid:that Abu Juhaifah said: \"I saw the Prophet (ﷺ), and Al-Hasan bin 'Ali resembles him the most","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2827-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2827-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2827-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd46","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2828,"bookHadithIndex":102,"text":"Narrated 'Ali:\"I did not hear the Prophet (ﷺ) mentioning both of his parents (that is including both in the saying \"May my father and mother be ransomed for you\") for anyone other than Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2828-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2828-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2828-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd47","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2829,"bookHadithIndex":103,"text":"Narrated 'Ali:\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not mention both of his parents for anyone except Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. On the Day of Uhud he said: 'Shoot, may my father and mother be ransomed for you.' And he said to him: 'Shoot! O young man","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2829-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Munkar"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2829-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Munkar"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2829-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd48","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2830,"bookHadithIndex":104,"text":"Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned both of his parents to me on the Day of Uhud","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2830-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2830-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2830-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2830-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd49","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2831,"bookHadithIndex":105,"text":"Narrated Anas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \"O my little son","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2831-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2831-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2831-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2831-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd4a","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2832,"bookHadithIndex":106,"text":"Narrated 'Amr bin Shu'aib:from his father, from his grandfather that the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered naming the child on the seventh day, removing the harm from him, and Al-'Aqq (removing the hair and slaughtering the animal for 'Aqiqah)","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2832-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2832-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2832-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2832-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd4b","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2833,"bookHadithIndex":107,"text":"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"The most loved names to Allah are 'Abdullah and 'Abdur-Rahman","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2833-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2833-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2833-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2833-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd4c","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2834,"bookHadithIndex":108,"text":"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"The most loved names to Allah are 'Abdullah and 'Abdur-Rahman","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2834-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd4d","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2835,"bookHadithIndex":109,"text":"Narrated 'Umar [bin Al-Khattab]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"I forbid naming with Rafi, Barakah and Yasar","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2835-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2835-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2835-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd4e","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2836,"bookHadithIndex":110,"text":"Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Do not name your boy Rabah, nor Aflah, nor Yasar, nor Najih, so that it may be said: 'Is he there?' and it may be said: 'No","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2836-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2836-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2836-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2836-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd4f","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2837,"bookHadithIndex":111,"text":"Narrated Al-A'raj:that Abu Hurairah conveyed to him that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"The most despicable (Akhna) name to Allah on the Day of Judgement is that of a man named King of Kings. (Malikil-Amlak)","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2837-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2837-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2837-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2837-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd50","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2838,"bookHadithIndex":112,"text":"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) changed the name of 'Asiyah, he said: \"You are Jamilah","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2838-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2838-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2838-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd51","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2839,"bookHadithIndex":113,"text":"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) would change abhorrent names","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2839-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2839-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2839-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd52","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2840,"bookHadithIndex":114,"text":"Narrated Muhammad bin Jubair bin Mut'im:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"I have some names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am Al-Mahi, the one by whom Allah wipes out disbelief, I am Al-Hasir, the one whom the people are gathered at his feet, and I am Al-'Aqib, the one after whom there is no Prophet","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2840-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2840-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2840-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2840-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd53","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2841,"bookHadithIndex":115,"text":"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited that one use his name and his Kunyah; naming themselves Muhammad Abul-Qasim","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2841-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2841-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2841-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2841-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd54","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2842,"bookHadithIndex":116,"text":"Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \"When you name yourself after me, then do not use my Kunyah","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2842-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2842-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2842-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2842-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd55","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2843,"bookHadithIndex":117,"text":"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that he said: \"O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! If I have a son after you do you think I could name him your Kunyah?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he said: \"So that was permitted for me","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2843-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2843-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2843-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2843-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd56","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2844,"bookHadithIndex":118,"text":"Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Indeed some poetry is wisdom","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2844-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2844-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2844-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd57","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2845,"bookHadithIndex":119,"text":"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Indeed some poetry is wisdom","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2845-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2845-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2845-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2845-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd58","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2846,"bookHadithIndex":120,"text":"Narrated 'Aishah:\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a Minbar placed in the Masjid for Hassan to stand to boast (poetically) about the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)\" - or she said: \"to defend the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed Allah has aided Hassan with the holy spirit (Jibril) as he boasts about - or - defends the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2846-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2846-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2846-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd59","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2846,"bookHadithIndex":121,"text":"(Another chain) from 'Aishah with the same narration","grades":[]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd5a","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2847,"bookHadithIndex":122,"text":"Narrated Anas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) entered Makkah during 'Umratil-Qada and 'Abdullah bin Rawahah was walking in front of him reciting verses of poetry. \"O tribes of disbelievers get out of his way - today we will strike you about its revelation; a strike that removes the heads from the shoulders - and makes the friend not concerned about his friend.\" 'Umar said to him: \"O Ibn Rawahah! Before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and in the sanctuary of Allah you utter poetry?\" the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Leave him O 'Umar! For it is quicker upon them than the raining arrow","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2847-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2847-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2847-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2847-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd5b","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2848,"bookHadithIndex":123,"text":"Narrated Al-Miqdam bin Shuraih:from his father, that 'Aishah was asked: \"Did the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say any poetry?\" She said: \"He would say parables with the poetry of Ibn Rawahah, saying: 'News shall come to you from where you did not expect it","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2848-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2848-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2848-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2848-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd5c","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2849,"bookHadithIndex":124,"text":"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"The best statement spoken by the Arab is the saying of Labid: 'Everything aside from Allah perishes","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2849-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2849-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2849-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2849-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd5d","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2850,"bookHadithIndex":125,"text":"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:\"I sat with the Prophet (ﷺ) more than one-hundred times. His Companions used to recite poetry and talk about things that occurred during Jahiliyyah, and he would remain silent, and sometimes he would smile along with them","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2850-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2850-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2850-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2850-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd5e","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2851,"bookHadithIndex":127,"text":"Narrated Muhammad bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"It is better that one of you fill his insides with puss than to fill it with poetry","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2851-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2851-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2851-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2851-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd5f","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2852,"bookHadithIndex":126,"text":"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"It is better that one of you fill his insides with puss than to fill it with poetry","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2852-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2852-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2852-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2852-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd60","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2853,"bookHadithIndex":128,"text":"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Indeed Allah detests the excessive among men, who slaps his tongue around like the cow slaps his tongue","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2853-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2853-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2853-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2853-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd61","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2854,"bookHadithIndex":129,"text":"Narrated Jabir:\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited that a man sleep on a terrace without something to obstruct him (so that he will not roll off and fall)","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2854-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2854-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2854-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd62","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2855,"bookHadithIndex":130,"text":"Narrated 'Abdullah:\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to take care of us by preaching during the days fearing that we may get bored","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2855-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2855-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2855-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd63","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2855,"bookHadithIndex":131,"text":"(Another chain) with similar meaning","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2855-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2855-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd64","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2856,"bookHadithIndex":132,"text":"Narrated Abu Salih:\"I asked 'Aishah and Umm Salamah about which deed did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) like to do most. They said: 'Whatever he could do regularly, even if it was little","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2856-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2856-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd65","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2856,"bookHadithIndex":133,"text":"It has been reported from Hisham bin 'Urwah from his father, that 'Aishah said:\"The most loved deed to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was what he could do regularly.\" (Another chain) with similar meaning","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2856-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd66","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2857,"bookHadithIndex":134,"text":"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Cover the vessels, tie the water-skins, close the doors, extinguish the torches, for indeed the mischief-makers (vermin) may drag away the wick, causing a fire for the inhabitants of the house","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2857-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2857-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2857-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2857-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0bd67","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":43,"hadithIndex":2858,"bookHadithIndex":135,"text":"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"When you travel through fertile land, then give the camels their fill of the land, and when you travel through drought, then hasten while they are fresh, and when you camp late, then stay away from the road, for indeed it is the route of the beasts and the abode of poisonous vermin in the night","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2858-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2858-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2858-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-43-2858-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]}]}